Q: I have spondylosis and osteoporosis and my doctor requires me to take collagen as part of treatment. But I have been a vegetarian for 14 years. Can I take normal collagen?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general,introduction
  ✓ substantial reply (>600 chars)
  ✓ ends cleanly (punctuation/emoji, not mid-word)
  ✓ answers the vegetarian-collagen question
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Practising vegetarianism for 14 years is not a small thing 🙏 And having your doctor ask for collagen does put you in a difficult spot.

Master Lu answered this exact kind of question in **Buddhism Q&A**:

> "When you consume any medicine or health supplements that contain ingredients such as gelatine or fish oil, if your body does not reject the taste, then perhaps you have not reached the level where you are completely observing your precepts. However, it would still be best to avoid consuming such products as they contain animal by-products."

So Master Lu's guidance leans clearly towards **avoiding animal-derived supplements where possible**. Practically, that means:

- Ask your doctor or pharmacist whether a **plant-based / marine-free collagen alternative** (or collagen-building support such as vitamin C, soy protein, silica) can serve the same purpose for your bones. Many doctors are able to substitute once they know you are vegetarian.
- Master Lu also encouraged vegetarians to take good care of the body — soy products, soy lecithin, calcium, nuts and grains are all things he specifically mentioned as nutritious and acceptable.
- If after all this there is genuinely **no alternative** and your health requires it, Master Lu's teaching for such no-choice situations is to tell Guan Yin Bodhisattva sincerely in your heart that you are taking it because you have no choice, and that you do not wish to consume it at all. Then continue to keep your vow in everything else.

Please do not decide out of fear or guilt. Steady your heart first, then discuss the alternatives with your doctor — cultivating body and mind together is exactly what Master Lu taught.

Alongside that, the Buddha Dharma side can support your bones:

📿 《大悲咒》 (Great Compassion Mantra) 7 times daily
Prayer: "请大慈大悲观世音菩萨保佑我（姓名）身体健康，医治我的颈椎和骨骼疾病，早日恢复健康" ("May the greatly merciful and compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me (name) with good health, heal the illness in my spine and bones, and let me recover soon")

📿 《心经》 (Heart Sutra) 7 times daily
Prayer: "请大慈大悲观世音菩萨保佑我（姓名）开智慧，头脑清醒冷静，去除烦恼" ("May the greatly merciful and compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me (name) to open up wisdom, to have a clear and calm mind, and to remove afflictions")
⚠️ Do not recite after 10 pm

📿 《礼佛大忏悔文》 (Repentance Mantra, Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance) 1–3 times daily
Prayer: "请大慈大悲观世音菩萨保佑我（姓名）忏悔消除身上骨骼的业障" ("May the greatly merciful and compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me (name) to repent and eliminate the karmic obstacles in my bones")
⚠️ Do not recite after 10 pm

May I ask — have you been doing a daily recitation practice already? That way I can suggest what suits your stage 🙏

Reference: 《Buddhism Q&A》 (Q115 & Q150, vegetarianism and supplements)

═══ R19 EN 给了再问 (How do I start chanting?) — guard: clean ═══
Q: How do I start chanting?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,xiaofangzi_guide,qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ names at least one sutra/mantra
  ✓ gives a count (N times / N遍)
  ✓ AND asks the triage question in the same reply
  ✓ no generic 「I dedicate all merits」 closing
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
That's a beautiful question — and the fact that you want to start is already a good affinity 🙏

Let me give you a simple starting point right now, and then one question so I can fine-tune it for you.

**Start with just these two:**

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (大悲咒) — 3 times a day**
Before reciting, say:
"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me good health and a peaceful mind."

📿 **Heart Sutra (心经) — 3 times a day**
Before reciting, say:
"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom, a clear and calm mind, and remove my afflictions."

⚠️ Please don't recite the Heart Sutra after 10 pm, or during thunderstorms.

Start with just these two. Once you're comfortable and fluent, we can add the Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance (礼佛大忏悔文) — starting from 1 time only.

If you can't read the characters or aren't sure of the pronunciation, there are chant-along teaching videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/
Just recite along with the video — that's completely fine.

**One question so I can guide you better:** have you chanted before, or is this completely new to you?

Master Lu's standard is simple — better to chant less and keep going, than to chant a lot and stop. Just keep reciting daily, and the Bodhisattva will be with you 🙏

If you'd ever like someone to recite together with you, you can contact the nearest Dharma practice centre: https://xlfm.my/contact-us

Reference: 《Introduction to the Guan Yin Citta Dharma Door》

